WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:14.562
"Who's Perda asked.

2
00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:16.283
"Come with us."

3
00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:18.965
The oldest girl blew at Zann and Darb.

4
00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:22.008
Zann felt his feet lifting off the ground.

5
00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:25.050
He struggled against the spell, but it was no use.

6
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.232
"You can't do this!"

7
00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:28.353
Gliss protested.

8
00:00:28.373 --> 00:00:29.994
"It's kidnapping!"

9
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:31.616
The girls giggled.

10
00:00:32.856 --> 00:00:33.537
"Come, cute dragon!"

11
00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:36.839
a younger girl cooed at Zing, who bounded along happily.

12
00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:39.942
"You'd better stop or else!"

13
00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:40.883
Perda warned.

14
00:00:41.623 --> 00:00:45.066
"We must show Mother," the oldest girl said calmly.

15
00:00:45.086 --> 00:00:48.549
"Halt!" Perda cried, rubbing her hands together.

16
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.392
Zann watched magic energy zip toward him and Darb.

17
00:00:53.173 --> 00:00:54.874
The tallest girl puffed out a breath.

18
00:00:55.915 --> 00:00:58.817
Bang! Perda's spell exploded and fizzled out.

19
00:00:58.837 --> 00:01:01.580
"Whoa." Perda sounded impressed.

20
00:01:02.188 --> 00:01:03.229
"How'd you do that?"

21
00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:05.951
"Come," the oldest girl said.

22
00:01:05.971 --> 00:01:07.592
"Let's find Mother."

23
00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:11.214
The girls walked away, with the boys floating beside them.

24
00:01:12.135 --> 00:01:15.117
"We shouldn't let them out of sight," Gliss told Perda.

25
00:01:16.077 --> 00:01:18.999
Zann felt powerless as he drifted through the forest.

26
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.362
Finally the whole group stopped at the base of an enormous tree.

27
00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.684
"Here we are," a girl said.

28
00:01:25.704 --> 00:01:30.487
"Home." She blew toward the ground and floated upward.

29
00:01:31.027 --> 00:01:31.788
So did her friends.

30
00:01:32.688 --> 00:01:36.971
Zann felt himself rise beside them, as Darb rose helplessly too.

31
00:01:37.991 --> 00:01:38.932
Zing flew along.

32
00:01:38.952 --> 00:01:40.893
"Wait!" Perda cried.

33
00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:42.114
"What about us?"

34
00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:44.295
"We'd better levitate."

35
00:01:44.575 --> 00:01:45.596
Gliss sounded nervous.

36
00:01:45.616 --> 00:01:48.397
"How high do you think they're going?"

37
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:51.559
"We'll bring you," the oldest girl said.

38
00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:53.200
"With your permission."

39
00:01:54.521 --> 00:01:55.702
Perda looked uncertain.

40
00:01:55.722 --> 00:01:57.523
"Um, okay.

41
00:01:57.963 --> 00:01:59.424
You have our permission."

42
00:02:00.496 --> 00:02:02.678
Soon Perda and Gliss were floating too.

43
00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:05.020
Perda ended up beside Zann.

44
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.962
"Are you okay?"

45
00:02:07.262 --> 00:02:07.762
she asked.

46
00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:09.444
He couldn't answer.

47
00:02:09.924 --> 00:02:11.165
He couldn't even nod his head.

48
00:02:12.106 --> 00:02:15.829
They floated up to a large, elaborate house built into the treetops.

49
00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.131
The girls led the way inside.

50
00:02:18.151 --> 00:02:20.793
"Mother!" the youngest cried.

51
00:02:20.813 --> 00:02:22.675
"Look what we found!"

52
00:02:23.736 --> 00:02:24.497
A woman looked up.

53
00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:30.462
She had green hair and skin like the girls, but her face was wrinkled and wise.

54
00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:33.724
"Ah, visitors," she said.

55
00:02:34.645 --> 00:02:36.746
"Have my girls immobilized you?

56
00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.028
My deepest apologies."

57
00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:43.231
She puffed out a breath, and Zann felt the spell dissipate.

58
00:02:43.251 --> 00:02:44.932
"Be careful, Mother!"

59
00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:45.813
a girl said.

60
00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:47.674
"They were trying to escape."

61
00:02:48.995 --> 00:02:49.836
Mother smiled.

62
00:02:50.397 --> 00:02:54.740
"Sit down, girls, and listen quietly while I talk with our visitors.

63
00:02:55.696 --> 00:02:58.318
This will be a learning opportunity for you."

64
00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:02.582
The girls sat down, watching with wide, curious eyes.

65
00:03:02.602 --> 00:03:08.026
"One thing they should do is learn not to immobilize people," Zann grumbled.

66
00:03:08.847 --> 00:03:09.587
Mother chuckled.

67
00:03:10.308 --> 00:03:12.230
"Please forgive my girls.

68
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.913
They've never left Zon, so they've never seen a male before.

69
00:03:17.754 --> 00:03:18.815
There are none here."

70
00:03:18.835 --> 00:03:21.177
"What about you?"

71
00:03:21.497 --> 00:03:22.098
Perda asked.

72
00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:24.620
"You don't seem surprised to see boys."

73
00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:29.611
"I traveled to many other worlds in my youth," Mother explained.

74
00:03:29.631 --> 00:03:31.433
"Can we keep them?"

75
00:03:31.813 --> 00:03:32.814
one of the girls asked.

76
00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:34.976
"I've always wanted a pet!"

77
00:03:35.896 --> 00:03:36.657
Mother smiled.

78
00:03:36.677 --> 00:03:40.080
"That wouldn't be right," she explained gently.

79
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.241
"Boys are people too."

80
00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.784
"Oh!" The girl looked disappointed.

81
00:03:45.804 --> 00:03:47.846
"If you say so, Mother."

82
00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:51.449
Zann wanted to get away from these strange females.

83
00:03:51.469 --> 00:03:54.471
"We refuse to be held prisoner!"

84
00:03:54.711 --> 00:03:56.789
he declared, trying to sound tough.

85
00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.812
"You're not prisoners," Mother said.

86
00:03:59.832 --> 00:04:02.254
"You're free to leave at any time."

87
00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:05.437
"Good." Zann stomped toward the door.

88
00:04:05.457 --> 00:04:06.838
"Come on, guys."

89
00:04:06.858 --> 00:04:08.780
"Wait," Gliss said.

90
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.942
"Mother seems to—to know things.

91
00:04:12.803 --> 00:04:14.044
Maybe she can help us."

92
00:04:15.405 --> 00:04:16.386
Zann hesitated.

93
00:04:16.847 --> 00:04:20.510
He still wanted to leave this place, but he realized Gliss was right.

94
00:04:21.451 --> 00:04:26.990
Mother seemed wise, and it was obvious that the people in this world had very strong magic.

95
00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:30.331
"Please stay," Mother urged.

96
00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:32.372
"At least for a little while.

97
00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:37.294
My girls rarely get the opportunity to learn from strangers."

98
00:04:37.314 --> 00:04:39.595
"Yes," a girl said.

99
00:04:39.615 --> 00:04:42.157
"We'd love to hear about your world."

100
00:04:42.177 --> 00:04:43.997
"All right."

101
00:04:44.397 --> 00:04:45.278
Zann sat down.

102
00:04:45.298 --> 00:04:52.701
"We come from Magica, and we're looking for my parents With help from his friends, he told the

103
00:04:52.741 --> 00:04:53.482
whole story.

104
00:04:54.523 --> 00:04:58.725
So we're checking every world with blue skies that we see," Zann finished.

105
00:04:59.206 --> 00:05:00.407
"That's how we landed here."

106
00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:02.528
Mother laughed heartily.

107
00:05:02.548 --> 00:05:05.090
"Oh, I'm sorry to laugh!"

108
00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.050
she exclaimed.

109
00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.553
"But there are more worlds out there than you can possibly imagine.

110
00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:15.356
Many of them—perhaps most—have blue skies.

111
00:05:16.577 --> 00:05:20.400
You could get lucky and find World X on your next try.

112
00:05:21.156 --> 00:05:24.197
Or you could spend the rest of your lives searching in vain."

113
00:05:25.378 --> 00:05:26.178
Zann frowned.

114
00:05:26.198 --> 00:05:27.699
"We have to try!"

115
00:05:28.659 --> 00:05:30.220
Mother smiled sympathetically.

116
00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.241
"I admire your spirit.

117
00:05:33.161 --> 00:05:34.222
Perhaps I can help.

118
00:05:34.742 --> 00:05:37.963
Do you have anything that belongs to the people you're seeking?"

119
00:05:39.264 --> 00:05:40.865
Zann pulled out his message stone.

120
00:05:40.885 --> 00:05:42.565
"This came from my parents."

121
00:05:42.585 --> 00:05:46.847
"Good." Mother leaned closer, blowing on the stone.

122
00:05:46.867 --> 00:05:51.563
"There. Now it should lead you straight to its rightful owners."

123
00:05:52.824 --> 00:05:53.985
"Really?" Zann said.

124
00:05:54.005 --> 00:05:55.886
"It'll take us to my parents?"

125
00:05:56.927 --> 00:05:58.468
"The spell never fails."

126
00:05:58.769 --> 00:06:00.010
Mother sounded confident.

127
00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.831
She turned to the girls.

128
00:06:02.452 --> 00:06:04.393
"Say good-bye to our visitors, girls.

129
00:06:04.994 --> 00:06:06.755
They must continue their quest."

130
00:06:06.775 --> 00:06:08.937
"Do they have to go?"

131
00:06:09.237 --> 00:06:09.858
a girl cried.

132
00:06:09.878 --> 00:06:12.120
"We want to hear more stories!"

133
00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.042
"Maybe another time," Perda said.

134
00:06:15.643 --> 00:06:16.924
Darb peered out a window.

135
00:06:17.344 --> 00:06:18.245
"How do we get down?

136
00:06:18.585 --> 00:06:20.166
And how will we find the wormhole?"

137
00:06:20.186 --> 00:06:22.548
"I can help with that too."

138
00:06:23.308 --> 00:06:24.449
Mother blew the door open.

139
00:06:24.469 --> 00:06:27.871
"Ready?" Zann and his friends nodded.

140
00:06:27.891 --> 00:06:30.193
"Come on, Zing," said Zann.

141
00:06:31.254 --> 00:06:33.455
Zing seemed reluctant to leave his new friends.

142
00:06:34.276 --> 00:06:37.878
But after more pats and kisses from the girls, he finally came to Zann.

143
00:06:37.898 --> 00:06:40.720
"Farewell and good luck."

144
00:06:41.361 --> 00:06:42.121
Mother blew at them.

145
00:06:43.062 --> 00:06:45.444
This time Zann didn't feel trapped by the spell.

146
00:06:46.356 --> 00:06:52.339
Mother's breath carried them gently but swiftly to the ground, through the forest, and finally to the wormhole.

147
00:06:52.359 --> 00:06:57.081
"Wow, that was weird," Perda said as they landed.

148
00:06:57.101 --> 00:06:59.542
"Yeah," Zann said.

149
00:06:59.562 --> 00:07:02.063
"But it worked out for the best, didn't it?"

150
00:07:03.323 --> 00:07:06.104
He reached into his pocket and touched his message stone.

151
00:07:06.945 --> 00:07:09.366
Would Mother's spell really lead him to his parents?

152
00:07:10.246 --> 00:07:14.188
Zann and his friends re-shackled themselves and then jumped through the wormhole.

153
00:07:15.132 --> 00:07:18.716
Zann gasped as the message stone suddenly yanked him forward.

154
00:07:19.637 --> 00:07:20.438
"It's working!"

155
00:07:20.658 --> 00:07:21.059
he cried.
